## State Management

### Decision tree

| Question                                  | Answer            |
| ----------------------------------------- | ----------------- |
| Is it from the database (Convex)?        | → Convex hooks    |
| Is it shared UI state?                   | → Zustand         |
| Is it form data?                         | → React Hook Form |
| Is it only used in one component?        | → useState        |
| Is it navigation state?                  | → Expo Router     |

### Convex (Server State)

Use Convex hooks for ALL database data:

```typescript
// features/users/hooks/use-user-data.ts
import { useQuery, useMutation } from 'convex/react';
import { api } from '@/convex/_generated/api';

export function useUserList(search?: string) {
  return useQuery(api.users.queries.list, { search });
}

export function useUpdateUser() {
  return useMutation(api.users.mutations.update);
}

// Usage in component
function UserList() {
  const users = useQuery(api.users.queries.list, { search: '' });

  // undefined = loading
  if (users === undefined) {
    return <LoadingSpinner />;
  }

  // null = no data
  if (users === null) {
    return <EmptyState />;
  }

  return <FlashList data={users} />;
}
```

### Zustand (UI State Only)

Use for shared UI state like modals, sheets, filters:

```typescript
// features/users/stores/user-ui-store.ts
import { create } from 'zustand';

interface UserUIState {
  searchQuery: string;
  isDeleteSheetOpen: boolean;
  deleteTargetId: string | null;
}

interface UserUIActions {
  setSearchQuery: (query: string) => void;
  openDeleteSheet: (userId: string) => void;
  closeDeleteSheet: () => void;
}

export const useUserUIStore = create<UserUIState & UserUIActions>(set => ({
  searchQuery: '',
  isDeleteSheetOpen: false,
  deleteTargetId: null,

  setSearchQuery: query => set({ searchQuery: query }),
  openDeleteSheet: userId =>
    set({ isDeleteSheetOpen: true, deleteTargetId: userId }),
  closeDeleteSheet: () =>
    set({ isDeleteSheetOpen: false, deleteTargetId: null }),
}));
```

### Avoiding Props Drilling

**Never pass props through multiple component levels.** If a prop needs to pass through 2+ components that don't use it, refactor:

```typescript
// ❌ Bad: Props drilling
<Parent userId={id}>
  <Layout userId={id}>        // doesn't use userId
    <Container userId={id}>   // doesn't use userId
      <UserCard userId={id} /> // finally uses it
    </Container>
  </Layout>
</Parent>

// ✅ Good: Call Convex directly
function UserCard({ userId }: { userId: Id<'users'> }) {
  const user = useQuery(api.users.queries.getById, { userId });
  // Direct access, no drilling
}
```

### Never do:

```typescript
// ❌ Don't duplicate Convex data in local state
const [users, setUsers] = useState([]);
const convexUsers = useQuery(api.users.queries.list);
useEffect(() => {
  if (convexUsers) setUsers(convexUsers);
}, [convexUsers]);

// ✅ Use Convex data directly
const users = useQuery(api.users.queries.list);
```

