## DRY Principle (Don't Repeat Yourself)

**Always look for opportunities to extract and reuse code.**

### Extract repeated logic into hooks

```typescript
// ✅ Good: Reusable hook
function useDebouncedSearch(defaultValue = '') {
  const [search, setSearch] = useState(defaultValue);
  const debouncedSearch = useDebounce(search, 300);
  return { search, setSearch, debouncedSearch };
}
```

### Extract repeated UI into components

```typescript
// ✅ Good: Reusable component
function StatusCard({ title, status, children }: StatusCardProps) {
  return (
    <Card>
      <CardHeader>
        <CardTitle>{title}</CardTitle>
        <Badge>{status}</Badge>
      </CardHeader>
      <CardContent>{children}</CardContent>
    </Card>
  )
}
```

### Extract repeated constants

```typescript
// ✅ Good: Centralized validation
export const commonSchemas = {
  name: z.string().min(2).max(100),
  email: z.string().email(),
  phone: z.string().regex(/^\+?[1-9]\d{1,14}$/),
};
```

### Before writing code, ask:

1. Does similar code exist elsewhere?
2. Will I need this logic again?
3. Is this UI pattern used elsewhere?
4. Are these values used elsewhere?

